Today I solved leetcode question 1721: Swapping Nodes in a Linked List.
Description: We are given a linked list along with an integer value k.
              We must swap node value at kth index from starting and kth index from ending.
              eg- [1,2,3,4,5] k=2
               ans=[1,4,3,2,5] ie. Linked list is 1 indexed.
Solution: First we create a 'temp' variable which will point towards head. Then another one with value 0 which we will call 'n'.
          And another two variables one being 'node1' which will point towards NULL and another 'val1' which will have val as -1.
          Then we will start our loop till the temp does not point towards NULL.
          With each loop we will add 1 to 'n' and take temp to next node.
          Once our 'n' reaches 'k' we will assign value to 'node1' as temp and 'val1' as value of temp.
          But we will continue our loop. Because we will get what is size of our linked list.
          Then again we will point 'temp' to head. And we will create two more variables 'node2' and 'val2'.
          We will then create a 'second' variable which will have value n-k. And then we will assign 'n' as 0.
          We will again start our loop till 'temp' reaches null. And if we reach a node where 'n==second' then we will assign values to 'node2' as temp and 'val2' as value of that node.
          Then we will end our loop. 
          And at last we will just assign values. Like we will change node1 value to val2 and node2 value to val1.
Time complexity- O(2n), Space Complexity-O(1)
